<% provide :page_title, t("morphosource.docs.contributors.title") %>

<h1 class="docs-title"><%= t("morphosource.docs.contributors.title") %></h1>

<div class="docs-content">
  <p>The most complete and up-to-date version of our documentation for contributor users and about contributor status is maintained at the <a href="https://wiki.duke.edu/display/MD/Contributor+User+Docs" target="_blank">MorphoSource Documentation Wiki</a>. Nonetheless, some of the information there is mirrored here for easy access.</p>
  
  <h2>What Is Contributor Status?</h2>

  <p>Contributor status is needed to <b>do the following actions</b> on MorphoSource:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>Upload new media</li>
    <li>Edit or delete existing media</li>
    <li>Create a new project or team</li>
    <li>Edit or delete existing projects or teams</li>
    <li>Participate in projects or teams</li>
    <li>Manage data that has been shared with you or transferred to you</li>
  </ul>

  <p>Contributor status is needed to <b>have the following Media User Roles</b> on MorphoSource (see <a href="https://wiki.duke.edu/display/MD/Definitions+of+User+Roles+for+Media" target="_blank">Definitions of User Roles for Media</a> on the full documentation wiki):</p>

  <ul>
    <li>Be the "Data Manager" of a Media record</li>
    <li>Be a "Data Editor" of a Media record</li>
  </ul>

  <p>Contributor status is needed to <b>have the following Project or Team Member Roles</b> on MorphoSource:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>Be a "Project/Team Manager" of a Project or Team Record</li>
    <li>Be a "Project/Team Editor" of a Project or Team Record</li>
    <li>Be a "Project/Team Depositor" of a Project or Team Record</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How To Become A Contributor</h2>

  <p>After creating a MorphoSource account, visit <a href="/contribute">Become A Contributor</a> and supply a few details about the media you intend to contribute to MorphoSource or your reason for applying to be a project member or data manager. An administrator will check your application, and you will either be approved or hear back with additional questions or instructions presently. Thank you!</p>

  <p>The specific information that will be requested from you when you apply for contributor status includes:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>The nature and purpose of the data you intend to contribute, or your reason for applying for project member and/or data manager status</li>
    <li>Organization (Institution, museum, university, etc.)</li>
    <li>Department</li>
    <li>If you are a graduate student, the name, email, and professional affiliation of your advisor</li>
    <li>Approximate size of the data you intend to contribute in gigabytes or other appropriate units</li>
  </ul>

  <p>You will also be asked to agree to the MorphoSource <a href="/contributor_terms" target="_blank">Contributor Terms of Use</a>. These are distinct from the general MorphoSource <a href="/terms" target="_blank">Terms of Use</a>, and you will be required to agree to comply with both sets of terms.</p>
</div>
